# Server configuration for the /contact form. Copy the names — never the values —
# into `.dev.vars` (gitignored) for local dev, and set them as Cloudflare Pages
# environment variables in production. Nothing real belongs in this repo.
#
# Everything else on the site stays static: donations are an outbound link to
# PayPal's hosted page, and the WhatsApp/email front door needs no secret.
#
# The form is deliberately fail-closed. With PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY unset the
# form isn't rendered at all; with TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY or the mail variables
# unset the endpoint refuses the submission and points people at WhatsApp. An
# unconfigured deployment is never an open relay to the org's inbox.

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile (bot challenge) -----------------------------------
# From the Turnstile dashboard. The site key is public by design — it ships in
# the page. The secret key never leaves the server.
# Cloudflare's always-passes test pair, useful for local work:
#   site   1x00000000000000000000AA
#   secret 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#
# PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY must be set as a Cloudflare Pages *build* variable,
# not only a runtime one: /contact is prerendered, so the key is baked into the
# HTML at build time. If it's missing at build, the form silently doesn't render
# and nothing errors. Rotating it needs a rebuild, not just an env change.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Resend (transactional email) -------------------------------------------
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL must be on a domain verified in the Resend account, or the
# send is rejected. It's the envelope sender only — the visitor's own address is
# set as Reply-To, so replying goes straight back to them.
RESEND_API_KEY=
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=
